<!--
    kuna C-surface normalization: a boolean-context comparison against zero
    renders in truthy form - `if (x != 0)` as `if (x)` and `if (p == 0)` as
    `if (!p)` (user-reported readability issue on the angr fmt corpus binary:
    `if (v8 != (char *)0x0)`; no upstream GH issue).

    Upstream Ghidra always renders the explicit comparison.  kuna adds the
    settable option `truthycond` (DIV-36, docs/history.md), default-on:
    the printer marks boolean contexts (if/while/for/ternary conditions,
    &&/||/! operands) with a CONDITION_CONTEXT mod and elides the eligible
    zero operand at INT_EQUAL/INT_NOTEQUAL.  Float compares, enum-typed and
    equate-named zeros keep the explicit form; value uses never rewrite.

    Stage model: S9 emission / condition-form policy.  P0 assertion:
    `option truthycond on|off`.

    tfn (0x100000): int4 tfn(int4 x) { if (x) return 7; return 3; }
      test edi,edi / jz +6 / mov eax,7 / ret / mov eax,3 / ret
    pfn (0x100020): int4 pfn(int8 *p) { if (!p) return 1; return *p; }
      test rdi,rdi / jnz +6 / mov eax,1 / ret / mov eax,[rdi] / ret

    vfn (0x100040, clang -O1 x86_64 of: int b = (x != 0); sink(b);
    return (x == 0)*3 + 4;): one `test edi,edi` feeds BOTH a setne (a VALUE
    consumed as a call argument) and a sete, so the setne lifts as
    BOOL_NEGATE over a shared INT_EQUAL that survives to print - the
    adversarial shape for the negate-absorption path.  A VALUE position must
    NEVER truthy-elide: `sink(x != 0)` would become `sink(x)` (5 instead of
    1 for x=5).  Asserts #5-#6 pin the value-safety in BOTH passes.

    Pass 1 (default): `if (x)` and `if (!p)` (asserts #1-#2, exactly once
    each; the explicit forms cannot match the truthy patterns).
    Pass 2 (option truthycond off): the explicit `if (x != 0)` and - with
    the DIV-34 NULL default - `if (p == NULL)` (asserts #3-#4).
-->
